# NEW PART = COPY: playing, switching (ARP held + a white key) to an EMPTY part copies the part you leave into it
# (events with their takes and frozen sounds, clip lengths, the part's bars and track mutes), as one undo step; a part with notes is
# never touched; no room: "NO ROOM" and the switch goes on; NEW PART = EMPTY: nothing is copied; stopped: nothing is copied
wait 300
tap SAVE
wait 100
tapkey w4
wait 200
expect nev 0
expect newpart 1
listen
# part A: six notes on track 1 (frozen sound 2), three on track 3, 2 bars, track 5 muted in the part
seed 0 1 6 2
seed 0 3 3 0
setbars 0 2
setpmask 0 16
expect nev 9
expect eventsA1 6
expect eventsB1 0
# stopped: choosing B is only choosing it (an empty part to compose in), nothing copied
press ARP
tapkey w1
release ARP
wait 100
expect part 1
expect eventsB1 0
expect nev 9
press ARP
tapkey w0
release ARP
wait 100
expect part 0
# playing: B is asked for; the copy is made at once, the switch waits for the bar's end
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 1
press ARP
tapkey w1
release ARP
wait 100
expect next 1
expect part 0
said A->B
expect eventsB1 6
expect eventsB3 3
expect eventsB2 0
expect nev 18
expect psndB1 2
expect psndA1 2
expect barsB 2
expect pmaskB 16
expect pmaskA 16
expect undo 3
wait 4600
expect part 1
expect playing 1
expect eventsA1 6
# a part with notes is never touched: C has two notes; asked for from B, it stays as it is
seed 2 1 2 0
setbars 2 3
expect nev 20
press ARP
tapkey w2
release ARP
wait 100
expect eventsC1 2
expect eventsC3 0
expect barsC 3
expect nev 20
wait 4600
expect part 2
# UNDO takes the copy away (D was empty): the clips, and the part's bars and mutes
setbars 3 6
press ARP
tapkey w3
release ARP
wait 100
expect eventsD1 2
expect barsD 3
expect nev 22
press EDIT
wait 800
release EDIT
wait 100
expect eventsD1 0
expect nev 20
expect barsD 6
# D is still asked for; the song goes there at the bar's end, empty
wait 4600
expect part 3
expect playing 1
# from an empty part nothing is copied; back to C (it has notes): untouched
press ARP
tapkey w2
release ARP
wait 100
expect nev 20
wait 4600
expect part 2
# a part asked for and changed our mind about, no edit in between: its copy is taken back
press ARP
tapkey w4
release ARP
wait 100
expect eventsE1 2
press ARP
tapkey w5
release ARP
wait 100
expect eventsE1 0
expect eventsF1 2
press ARP
tapkey w2
release ARP
wait 100
expect eventsF1 0
expect nev 20
wait 4600
expect part 2
# NEW PART = EMPTY: the old way, nothing copied
newpart 0
press ARP
tapkey w6
release ARP
wait 100
expect eventsG1 0
expect next 6
wait 4600
expect part 6
# back to C
newpart 1
press ARP
tapkey w2
release ARP
wait 4600
expect part 2
# no room: the pool full (part H holds the ballast): the copy is skipped, NO ROOM, the switch still happens
ballast 4090
expect nev 4096
said
press ARP
tapkey w4
release ARP
wait 100
said NO ROOM
expect eventsE1 0
expect next 4
expect nev 4096
wait 4600
expect part 4
expect playing 1
